From: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] corenetwork: declare agentgateway_mgmt_port_t on TCP 15000, 15020-15021

agentgateway always opens three management listeners besides its data
listener: admin on 15000, stats on 15020 and readiness on 15021
(agentgateway d204f9c, crates/agentgateway/src/config.rs). None of the
three numbers is declared in this file, so they fall into
unreserved_port_t, which agentgateway_t may not bind; in its own domain
the gateway could not start. A port type of its own keeps the grant to
these three numbers instead of every unreserved port. The TactiQ OS
config binds all three to 127.0.0.1.

Checked against refpolicy main: no port or range here covers 15000,
15020 or 15021. Applies on top of 0001 and 0004.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [TactiQ OS specific service]

Signed-off-by: TactiQ OS <andrey@tactiq.ai>
---
 policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in b/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in
--- a/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in
+++ b/policy/modules/kernel/corenetwork.te.in
@@ -94,5 +94,6 @@
 network_port(afs3_callback, tcp,7001,s0, udp,7001,s0)
 network_port(agentgateway, tcp,49317,s0)
+network_port(agentgateway_mgmt, tcp,15000,s0, tcp,15020-15021,s0)
 network_port(tactiq_stop, tcp,49318,s0)
 network_port(agentx, udp,705,s0, tcp,705,s0)
 network_port(amanda, udp,10080-10082,s0, tcp,10080-10083,s0)
